.TH NGINX-MON 1 "July 2026" "nginx-mon 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nginx-mon \- real-time Nginx reverse-proxy traffic monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nginx-mon
.RI [ --log-file " PATH" ]
.RI [ --refresh-interval " SECONDS" ]
.RI [ --max-records " COUNT" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nginx-mon
tails an Nginx JSON access log and displays upstream traffic grouped by
frontend virtual host. It retains a bounded in-memory request history and does
not modify Nginx logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --log-file PATH
JSON access log to follow. Unless discovery is requested, the default is
.IR /var/log/nginx/nginx-mon-access.json.log .
.TP
.B --detect-nginx
Locate one running Nginx master and follow its only open, nonempty access log
that matches nginx-mon's JSON log format. This Linux-only convenience reads
.IR /proc ;
it does not execute Nginx or parse its configuration. If discovery is
ambiguous or no matching log has traffic yet, use
.BR --log-file .
.TP
.B --nginx-pid PID
Locate the monitor log for the specified running Nginx master process. This
also enables discovery. An explicit
.B --log-file
takes precedence over both discovery options.
.TP
.B --refresh-interval SECONDS
Positive table refresh interval. The default is 1 second.
.TP
.B --max-records COUNT
Positive number of recent requests retained for the detail view. The default
is 5000.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up/Down
Move through frontend rows or detail rows.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the requests for the highlighted frontend.
.TP
.B Escape
Return from request detail to the live frontend table.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the log and table immediately.
.TP
.B p
Pause or resume live log ingestion and table updates. The displayed traffic is
frozen while paused.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl-C
Quit the monitor.
.SH NGINX LOG FORMAT
Install the supplied
.IR nginx_mon.conf
under Nginx's included configuration directory. It writes JSON records using
the upstream byte variables. Backend TX is
.BR $upstream_bytes_sent ,
the bytes Nginx sent to the upstream. Backend RX is
.BR $upstream_bytes_received ,
the bytes Nginx received from the upstream. A request with multiple upstream
attempts can contain comma-separated values; nginx-mon sums them.
.PP
The detail view also displays the TCP source endpoint from
.BR $remote_addr : $remote_port ,
the Nginx listener port from
.BR $server_port ,
and TLS protocol from
.BR $ssl_protocol .
.PP
The monitor uses the listener address from
.BR $server_addr
with NetworkManager to display the active network connection name, for example
.IR ens18 .
If NetworkManager does not own the interface, the interface name is used;
unavailable network information is shown as a dash.
An empty SSL protocol is displayed as Plain. When Nginx is behind another
proxy, configure its real IP module to log the original client address.
.PP
For a source-built Nginx, put the supplied log format in the existing
.B http
configuration and its access log directive in the deployed proxy server. The
sample test server and its RPM paths are not required. The account running
.B nginx-mon
must be able to read the access log and the selected process descriptors under
.IR /proc .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/nginx-mon/nginx_mon.conf
Sample Nginx log format and reverse-proxy server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nginx (8)
